// Skills NPCs can train. A recipe's `skill` must name one of these (an unknown
// name is a load error, not a silently-created phantom skill).
//
//   name  display / lookup id
//   gain  proficiency gained each time the skill is used
//   cap   maximum proficiency
[
    (name: "farming", gain: 0.02, cap: 5.0),
    (name: "baking",  gain: 0.02, cap: 5.0),
    // The trade of the dead: cutting the grey reeds of the fen and weaving them into the
    // burial shrouds a purgatory never wants for. A wholly data-defined calling — the
    // planner finds it like any other, and a "weaver" emerges with no Rust changes. It
    // feeds money, not bellies (a shroud is inedible), so it never starves the food loop:
    // a soul must still eat bread.
    (name: "weaving", gain: 0.02, cap: 5.0),
    // The delver's trade: drawing ore from the dead rock and working it through to a finished
    // tool — one calling spanning a three-step chain (delve → smelt → forge), so a division of
    // labour can emerge *within* a single craft. Inedible, like the weaver's: money, not bread.
    (name: "delving", gain: 0.02, cap: 5.0),
]
